ROCm::Inference
===============

Perl binding of libinference, the zero-copy LLM inference engine of the rocm-hip repository for AMD Strix Halo
(gfx1151, ROCm): Qwen3.5 / Qwen3.6 (dense and MoE) and Qwen3.8-Flash-Next with MTP speculative decoding, GGUF
models memory-mapped in place, a KV block store of mmap()ed files shared between processes.

The XS maps the C API function by function (the model handle first); chat templates are rendered in Perl with
the Minijinja module; the KV store's policy (eviction, disk tier) is ROCm::Inference::Store.

INSTALLATION

    perl Makefile.PL
    make
    make test
    make install

Makefile.PL finds libinference through ROCM_INFERENCE_PREFIX (an installed copy, `make install PREFIX=...` in
rocm-hip), pkg-config (rocm-inference), or the rocm-hip checkout the module sits in (perl/ROCm-Inference),
building libinference.so there when needed (ROCm / hipcc).

chat_render / chat need the Minijinja module 0.1.1 or later (Perl XS over the Rust minijinja library). In a
rocm-hip checkout it is the perl-minijinja-xs submodule:

    git submodule update --init perl-minijinja-xs
    cd perl-minijinja-xs && bash scripts/setup-minijinja.sh && perl Makefile.PL && make && make install

Tests beyond t/00-load.t need the GPU and models, given by environment variables:

    ROCM_INFERENCE_TEST_MODEL=/path/Qwen3.5-4B-ROCMFP4.gguf
    ROCM_INFERENCE_TEST_QWEN38=/path/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-...-00001-of-00003.gguf
    ROCM_INFERENCE_TEST_DRAFT=/path/mtp-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Q4_0_ROCMFP4_FAST.gguf

